  "descriptionMarkdown": "So I decided to bring you everything you need to built your belt arrays. This will be the last part of series of multiple Blueprints books I am going to post. Split-off/Priority Splitters/Separators. Going: Yellow, Red, Blue, Yellow.\n\nEverything was named and categorized in such a way as to help to navigate and recognize the blueprints with just as single sight of them.\n\nBP's included (+inverted versions for a complete total of 20 BP's):\n\n--Belt Lane Separator\n\n--4-Belt Split-off (mechanical prioritization)\n\n--4-Belt Two-sided Balanced Split-off\n\n--4-Belt One-sided Balanced Split-off\n\n--2-Belt Split-off (mechanical prioritization)\n\n--4-Belt Internally Balanced Split-off (mechanical prioritization)\n\n--4-Belt One-sided Internally Balanced COMPACT Split-off (mechanical prioritization)\n\n--4-Belt Two-sided Internally Balanced COMPACT Split-off (mechanical prioritization)\n\n--Belt Circuit Priority Splitter Segment (up belt priority)\n\n--Belt Circuit Priority Splitter Segment (down belt priority)\n\n--Belt Circuit Priority Splitter Split-off Segment\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nUSER MANUAL FOR PRIORITY SPLIT OFF'S:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PZMUtcztWeE\n\nhttps://forums.factorio.com/viewtopic.php?f=18&t=47050&p=272829#p272829\n\nhttps://forums.factorio.com/viewtopic.php?f=202&t=32817\n\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nCredits should go, but are not limited, to the following REDDIT'ors and FORUM'ers:\n\nRedditNamesAreShort - 12to12, 24to24 balancers, Yet Another Belt Balancer Compendium; MadZuri - 8to8, Universal8to8, Belt balancer compendium; Yttrium - Ytterby Balancer; QonQon - Fractal Balancers; ICantThinkOfABetterUsername - Imgur Belt Balancer Compendium; [deleted] - Count Perfect N to M Belt Balancers; ribsngibs - Further development of 8+ balancers and Fractal Balancer idea; Steejo and Arumba - Priority Spliter Makers/Testers; Lord_Peppe - Further refinement of the Priority Splitter; jhg300 - Priority splitter development;\n",
